(Page 1: Retrieval-Augmented Generation Architecture) Tj T*
T*
(Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) is an artificial intelligence) Tj T*
(framework that enhances large language models by dynamically retrieving) Tj T*
(relevant facts from authoritative external knowledge bases before) Tj T*
(synthesizing a response.) Tj T*
T*
(In standard RAG architectures, knowledge retrieval bridges the gap between) Tj T*
(static parametric weights learned during pre-training and private, dynamic,) Tj T*
(or domain-specific enterprise documents.) Tj T*
T*
(The document ingestion pipeline executes three primary phases: document) Tj T*
(text extraction, document chunking into bounded passages, and index) Tj T*
(construction. Document chunking partitions multi-page PDFs into overlapping) Tj T*
(word segments, typically targeting 120 words with 30-word overlaps to) Tj T*
(maintain contextual continuity across chunk boundaries.) Tj T*
T*
(By grounding model generation in retrieved passages, RAG systems) Tj T*
(dramatically mitigate generative hallucinations, provide verifiable) Tj T*
(page-level audit trails, and eliminate the prohibitive cost of continuous) Tj T*
(model fine-tuning.) Tj T*
T*
