(Page 2: Vector Embeddings and TF-IDF Retrieval) Tj T*
T*
(Information retrieval in RAG platforms relies on either dense vector) Tj T*
(embeddings, sparse lexical retrieval, or hybrid combinations.) Tj T*
T*
(Dense retrieval encodes textual passages into high-dimensional continuous) Tj T*
(vector spaces using neural embedding models. In contrast, sparse lexical) Tj T*
(retrieval utilizes Term Frequency Inverse Document Frequency \(TF-IDF\) and) Tj T*
(BM25 algorithms, calculating term importance based on statistical) Tj T*
(distribution across document chunks.) Tj T*
T*
(The TF-IDF retrieval engine scores candidate passages using cosine) Tj T*
(similarity between the expanded query vector and precomputed chunk vectors.) Tj T*
(Cosine similarity evaluates the cosine of the angle between two non-zero) Tj T*
(vectors in inner product space, yielding normalized scores between 0.0 and) Tj T*
(1.0.) Tj T*
T*
(To bridge vocabulary mismatches, acronym-aware query expansion discovers) Tj T*
(dynamic abbreviations such as NLP \(Natural Language Processing\) and RAG) Tj T*
(within the corpus, enriching short queries before matrix multiplication.) Tj T*
T*
